{{also|VOX|VOx}}
==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Indo-European|wōkʷs|speech, voice|lang=la}}. Cognates include {{etyl|sa|-}} {{term|sc=Deva|वाच्|tr=vā́c|lang=sa}} and {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|sc=polytonic|ὄψ|tr=óps|lang=grc}}. {{proto|Indo-European|wōkʷ-|lang=}} is an [[o-grade]] of {{proto|Indo-European|wekʷ-|title=|lang=}}, which is where {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|ἔπος|tr=épos|lang=grc}} came from.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/woːks/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-vox.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|vōx|vocis#Latin|vōcis|f|third}}

# [[voice]]
# [[accent]]
# [[speech]], [[remark]]
# {{grammar|lang=la}} [[voice]]; indicating the relation of the subject of the verb to the action which the verb expresses
# {{inflection of|vox||voc|s}}

